  "notes": "{縮|ちぢ}む is intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}). The transitive pair is {縮|ちぢ}める (to shrink something).\n\nASPECT ({ている}):\n{縮|ちぢ}んでいる indicates a resulting state of having shrunk, not an ongoing process.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- セーターが{縮|ちぢ}む (sweater shrinks)\n- {距離|きょり}が{縮|ちぢ}む (distance shortens)\n- {身|み}が{縮|ちぢ}む (to cringe, feel small)\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- ～が{縮|ちぢ}む: The subject that shrinks\n\nThe related verb {縮|ちぢ}まる also means \"to shrink\" but emphasizes a more complete or natural contraction. {縮|ちぢ}む is more general.",
